---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout title="Delete Your Account — Foremann" description="How to delete your Foremann account, what data is removed, and what we're required to keep.">
  <Nav />

  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="display">Delete Your Account</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Foremann is a business texting and calling app for tradespeople, operated by
        Minium LLC. This page explains how to delete your Foremann account, exactly what
        data is removed, and the few things we're required to keep.
      </p>
      <div class="legal-meta">Last updated: July 30, 2026</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-body">
    <div class="wrap legal-doc">

      <h2>1. Delete your account from the app</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <strong>Foremann</strong> and sign in.</li>
        <li>Go to the <strong>Settings</strong> tab.</li>
        <li>Scroll to the bottom and tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
        <li>Confirm when prompted.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Deletion starts immediately and <strong>cannot be undone</strong>. There is no
        grace period and no way for us to restore the account afterwards.
      </p>

      <h2>2. If you can't sign in</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:privacy@foremann.app">privacy@foremann.app</a> from the
        email address on your account, or tell us the phone number you signed up with.
        We'll verify that you own the account and delete it within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What gets deleted</h2>
      <p>Deleting your account permanently removes all of the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your profile:</strong> name, email address, personal phone number, time zone, and your sign-in credentials.</li>
        <li><strong>Your business profile:</strong> business name, trade, service area, pricing notes, availability, and tone preferences.</li>
        <li><strong>Your client records:</strong> every customer name, phone number, address, note, and contact photo you saved.</li>
        <li><strong>Your message history:</strong> the full body of every text sent to and from your business number, along with all photos and file attachments.</li>
        <li><strong>Your call history:</strong> call logs, voicemails, call recordings, and transcripts. Recording audio is deleted from our storage and from our telephony provider.</li>
        <li><strong>AI content:</strong> every draft reply, follow-up, and summary generated for your account.</li>
        <li><strong>Text-messaging consent records:</strong> opt-in and opt-out events recorded for your clients.</li>
        <li><strong>Push notification tokens</strong> for every device you signed in on.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        At the same time, your <strong>subscription is cancelled</strong> so you are not
        billed again, and your <strong>Foremann business phone number is released</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Your business phone number can't be recovered</h2>
      <p>
        Once released, your business number returns to the carrier's pool and may be
        reassigned to someone else. If you want to keep that number, port it to another
        carrier <em>before</em> you delete your account. We can't retrieve it afterwards.
      </p>

      <h2>5. What we keep, and for how long</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Encrypted backups:</strong> deleted data may persist in our encrypted backups for up to 30 additional days before rotating out. Backups are used only for disaster recovery and are never used to restore a deleted account.</li>
        <li><strong>Billing records:</strong> our payment processor (Stripe) retains invoice and transaction records as required by tax and accounting law. These contain your billing history, not your messages or client data.</li>
        <li><strong>Carrier records:</strong> our telephony provider (Twilio) keeps its own message and call logs to meet telecom record-keeping requirements, on their retention schedule.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Deleting some data without deleting your account</h2>
      <p>
        You don't have to delete your whole account to remove data. In the app you can
        delete an individual conversation, which removes its messages and attachments.
        Deleted messages are held for a 30-day grace period and are then permanently
        purged. You can also delete individual client records and their notes.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:privacy@foremann.app">privacy@foremann.app</a>. For anything
        else, see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Mirrors the scoped legal styles in privacy.astro / terms.astro. Astro
     scopes <style> per component, so these can't be inherited — they're
     duplicated deliberately. Keep the three legal pages in sync. */
  .legal-hero {
    padding: clamp(60px, 8vw, 100px) 0 clamp(30px, 4vw, 50px);
  }
  .legal-hero .display {
    font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px);
    margin: 18px 0 20px;
  }
  .legal-hero .lede { max-width: 720px; }
  .legal-meta {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .legal-body {
    padding: clamp(30px, 5vw, 60px) 0 clamp(60px, 9vw, 120px);
  }
  .legal-doc {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .legal-doc h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 28px);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 56px 0 14px;
  }
  .legal-doc h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal-doc h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
  }
  .legal-doc p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  /* `ol` is added here — the other legal pages only use `ul`, but the
     deletion steps are numbered and Play expects them to read as steps. */
  .legal-doc ul,
  .legal-doc ol {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .legal-doc li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .legal-doc strong { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  .legal-doc a {
    color: var(--rust);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .legal-doc a:hover { color: var(--rust-dark); }
  .legal-doc code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--sand);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
